  "id": "drystore12",
  "note": "DRY STORE 12 — a plain dry-goods warehouse on Kessler Street.\n\nThe tile's prose: concrete-floored, echoing, racking bolted to the ceiling, DRY STORE 12 painted\non the roller door in fading yellow. Cheap to hold, steady to run.\n\nSo it is a portal-framed shed in corrugated sheet under a barrel roof, with the frame showing as\nsteel piers, one big roller door with a loading canopy over it, a personnel door beside it, and the\nstore number painted above the door rather than on it. High strip windows light the racking. A\nworks doesn't sign itself (UNSIGNED_TRADE), so the number is the only lettering.",
